{"availability":"available","full":"mmomtchev/sqlite-wasm-http","name":"sqlite-wasm-http","description":"An experimental HTTP VFS driver for SQLite WASM","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":160,"forks":9,"created":"2023-03-04T17:35:44Z","updated":"2026-10-13T21:14:20Z","license":"ISC","branch":"main","homepage":"https://sqlite-wasm-http.momtchev.com","topics":[],"demo":"https://sqlite-wasm-http.momtchev.com/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T21:15:38.132Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T21:15:38.132Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T21:15:38.132Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T19:51:48.409Z","stars":160,"forks":9},{"at":"2026-10-17T21:15:38.132Z","stars":160,"forks":9}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["This project is inspired by @phiresky/sql.js-httpvfs but uses the new official SQLite WASM distribution.","It includes a number of improvements over the first version:","The shared cache version uses SharedArrayBuffer which requires that the server hosting the JS code sends Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin and Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp headers (aka CORS 2)."],"features":["Based upon what will probably be the industry reference (backed by SQLite and Google)","Supports multiple concurrent connections to the same database with shared cache","Simplified fall-back version without support for sharing cache between worker threads that does not require SharedArrayBuffer","Aims to support all bundlers out-of-the-box without special configuration","a more modern one, that uses a dedicated HTTP worker thread to run asynchronously all HTTP operations for all SQLite3 workers and implements sharing of the cache between those"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/mmomtchev/sqlite-wasm-http/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"8a93c5e5441db9488c9745aa38fb644bfc5a9faf7d77e2182e2e672bb501b299","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:48.543Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:48.543Z","projectI